    "type": "message",
    "user": "U08S5BR47GA",
    "text": "Hi \u003c@U0CA4S2GS4B\u003e, this is expected behaviour right now. Complex Postgres types like `jsonb` ,`text[]`, etc. are written as strings. The full source-to-destination type mapping is here: \u003chttps://olake.io/docs/connectors/postgres/#data-type-mapping|olake.io/docs/connectors/postgres#…\u003e\n\n\nthe variant support is on our roadmap and will be releasing support for it in coming months. You can create a issue for the same on olake repo as well\n\u003chttps://github.com/datazip-inc/olake/issues|github.com/datazip-inc/olake/issues\u003e",
    "ts": "1793797244.199049",
    "thread_ts": "1793795890.072239",
